# Direct push and merge

Whenever meaningful code changes are completed in this repo:

1. Commit on the current feature branch (concise message, only related files).
2. Push the branch to `origin`.
3. Create a PR into `main` (if none is open) and **merge it immediately** (`gh pr merge --merge`).
4. Report the PR URL when done.

Do not wait for a separate “commit / push / merge” request unless the user explicitly says not to merge yet.

If Smart Mode blocks merging to `main`, retry with approval using the exact block reason — the user has pre-authorized this workflow.
